<section class="page-hero"><span class="pub-kicker">See StockChief in action</span><h1>Take a closer look<br>at the real operation.</h1><p>A <%= Math.floor(demo.durationMilliseconds/60000) %>-minute guided recording of the actual StockChief application, with reproducible demonstration records.</p></section><section class="truth-recording"><video controls preload="metadata" poster="/demo/inventory.png?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" aria-label="Recorded StockChief product walkthrough"><source src="/demo/<%= demo.video %>?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" type="video/webm"><track kind="captions" src="/demo/walkthrough.vtt?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" srclang="en" label="English" default>Your browser can download the <a href="/demo/<%= demo.video %>">product walkthrough</a>.</video><p>Captured in <%= demo.business %>. Stock comes from recorded movements; purchase orders remain distinct from physical receipts.</p></section><section class="truth-demo-chapters"><% const copy={inventory:'See the product, stock by location and the movements behind its balance.',planning:'Review planning evidence, including when more demand history is needed.',purchasing:'Review an actual purchase order and the quantity still expected.',ask:'See an answer read from the same PostgreSQL business records.',brief:'Return to the owner’s Home view and the work needing attention.',import:'Review preserved fields and stock quantities before approving any changes.'};for(const scene of demo.screens){ %><article data-reveal><figure><img loading="lazy" src="/demo/<%= scene.file %>?v=<%= locals.assetVersion||'current' %>" alt="Actual StockChief screen: <%= scene.title %>" width="1440" height="900"></figure><h2><%= scene.title %></h2><button type="button" data-video-chapter="<%= Math.floor(scene.atMilliseconds/1000) %>">Watch this chapter</button><p><%= copy[scene.file.split('.')[0]] %></p></article><% } %></section><section class="qualification-note"><h2>What this demonstration proves</h2><p>These are captures of the current application in a fresh, controlled PostgreSQL business. The recording uses synthetic records and a deterministic test classifier; the displayed answer comes from those business records. Merchant payments, carrier delivery and mailbox events require separate provider verification.</p></section><section class="truth-final"><p class="pub-kicker">Bring your own operation</p><h2>See the fit.<br>Choose your plan.</h2><div class="pub-actions"><a class="pub-btn" href="/pricing">Compare plans</a><a class="pub-btn pub-btn--secondary" href="/capabilities">Explore capabilities</a></div></section>
